  "body": "# \n\nensure pre-insertion validity (https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-ensure-pre-insertion-validity)\n6. doctype\n \"parent has a doctype child, an element is preceding child, or child is null and parent has an element child.\" << \"preceding\" operates on two object (nodes) but here `child` can be `null` so it's strange. Maybe write \"...,child is not null and element is preceding child,...\"  \nAnd maybe clarify some things in this three condition:\n\"doctype is following child.\" << we don't see what exactly \"doctype\" is, so better use \"doctype in/inside/from parent\" or write full prose \"parent has a doctype which is following child\"\n\"element is preceding child\" << like above, better use \"element in//inside/from parent\"\n# \n\nhttps://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-node-normalize\nOne typo, in greenbox above we have ()().\n",
